<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">beastlord</ansi>

The Beastlord is the neutral elite of the Bearward (Beast Tamer route; no
alignment asked). Its bear swipes two foes at once, guards more often, and
once a battle stands back up after it falls.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Ranks</ansi>

  30 Cleaving swipe     the bear's blows also strike the foe beside its target
                        for half the damage
  35 Great bear         the bear has 160% of a wolf's health
  40 Heavy paws         +3 damage on the bear's blows (in all)
  45 Faithful guard     the bear guards six times a battle
  50 Raking swipe       the bear's second foe takes three quarters of the
                        damage
  55 Elder bear         the bear has 190% of a wolf's health
  60 Stands again       once a battle, a bear that falls stands back up with
                        half its health

It needs the Bearward first (<ansi fg="command">help beasttamer-routes</ansi>) and keeps every rank of it. At level 30 a
character that holds it promotes with <ansi fg="command">class promote [member] beastlord confirm</ansi>. Any alignment may take it.
Everything here lasts only for the battle and is never saved.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Elite talents</ansi>

Elite Beast Tamer talents (levels 35, 45, 55): Iron Hide (+5 Armor), Pack
Bond (your beast has 15% more health), Savage Jaws (+2 damage on your
beast's blows). See <ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help beasttamer-routes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help beasttamer</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help elite</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help promotion</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>.
